      "runs": {
        "centaur-aux-lamps-in-play": {
          "note": "Each top-lane closure lit one lane lamp: public 5 (printed TOP LEFT LANE) lit 97, public 4 (TOP MIDDLE LANE) lit 81, and public 3 (TOP RIGHT LANE) completed the three lanes, which left every lane lamp dark, and on the cleared lanes lit 65. The shared flipper-button switch 21 rotated the lit lane through 65, 81 and 97 (press 1: lit 81, extinguished 65; press 2: lit 97, extinguished 81; press 3: lit 65, 113, extinguished 97; press 4: lit 81, extinguished 65, 113; press 5: lit 97, extinguished 81; press 6: lit 65, 113, extinguished 97); whenever the lit lane wrapped from 97 to 65 the ROM also raised 113 in the same update and cleared it again with 65 on the next rotation, so 113 is the carry bit of a four-bit top-lane register. Over the whole run lamp 113 changed 18 times as part of power-up and game-start lamp flashes, in each of which it and at least three other lamps of its lamp-data line PD3 or of lamp address 0 made the same change in one update, every lighting put out again by the same group within 0.3 s, and 3 times with 65 at a lane rotation, and never otherwise. A struck slingshot or thumper bumper flicked its own lamp off and back on and fired its own coil: 37 flicked 66 and fired 13, 38 flicked 82 and fired 12, 39 flicked 98 and fired 11, and 40 flicked 114 and fired 10. Every one of these is derived from the lamp and solenoid events of the retained trace by tools/centaur_aux_lamp_runtime_summary.py, which refuses a trace that does not show it."
        }
      },
